config COMET_GAMEPAD_COMBO_MAX
	int "Maximum number of button combinations"
	default 8
	range 1 32
	help
	  Number of button combinations that can be set up. Each one needs a small work item.

config COMET_GAMEPAD_COMBO_POWER_UP_WINDOW_MS
	int "Time after power-up for the power-up combinations"
	default 1000
	range 100 10000
	help
	  A combination that is made at power-up is only looked for when all of its buttons are
	  pressed within this time after power-up, in milliseconds. Pressing them later does
	  nothing, so a game cannot start it by accident.

config COMET_GAMEPAD_COMBO_STACK_SIZE
	int "Stack size of the combination work queue"
	default 1024
	help
	  The actions of the combinations run in their own work queue, because some of them
	  block, for example to erase flash or to restart. That would stop the system work
	  queue, which also drives the status LED.

config COMET_GAMEPAD_COMBO_THREAD_PRIORITY
	int "Priority of the combination work queue"
	default 10
	help
	  Thread priority of the work queue that runs the actions of the combinations.
